/target
Cargo.lock
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
# Stray recordings: `claudectl --record demo.gif` and `asciinema rec` both write
# their output to whatever directory you ran them from. Ignore those by default…
*.cast
*.gif
# …but never the committed assets. Without these negations `git add -A` skips a
# new asset without a word: #515 shipped a README pointing at a GIF that was
# never committed, and main served a broken hero image until #516 fixed it.
# Everything tracked today had to be `git add -f`'d past the two lines above.
!assets/**/*.gif
!assets/**/*.cast
!docs/assets/**/*.gif
!docs/assets/**/*.cast
# Demo media committed at the repo root, from before assets/ existed.
!/claude-demo.gif
!/claudectl.gif
!/demo.cast
!/demo.gif
GROWTH.md
.claudectl-runs/
social/

# Added by cargo
#
# already existing elements were commented out

